# Git & Workflow Rules

## Lovable Sync

This project is connected to [Lovable](https://lovable.dev). Commits pushed to the connected branch sync back to the Lovable editor.

### Never

- Force push to connected branches
- Rebase, amend, or squash commits already pushed to remote
- Rewrite published git history

### Always

- Keep the branch in a working state (buildable)
- Create new commits for fixes (don't amend pushed commits)
- Run lint before committing when possible

## Commit Guidelines

- Only commit when explicitly requested
- Write concise commit messages focusing on **why**, not what
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, API keys, credentials)
- Do not commit unless asked

## Branch Workflow

- Feature work on branches (Lovable may use main directly)
- Do not force push to main/master
- Pull before starting work if collaborating

## Files to Never Edit Manually

| File | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `src/routeTree.gen.ts` | Auto-generated by TanStack Router |
| `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts` | Auto-generated |
| `src/integrations/supabase/auth-middleware.ts` | Auto-generated |
| `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` | Auto-generated (regenerate after migrations) |

## Pre-Commit Checks

```sh
npm run lint    # ESLint
npm run build   # Verify build (when making significant changes)
```

## Scope Discipline

- One concern per commit/PR when possible
- Do not mix documentation changes with feature changes unless requested
- Do not reformat unrelated files
